 "wanderers": {
  "rule": "W wanderers are kept alive (hired included, as vanilla counts them); SwapCompanions is kept; TryKillCompanion never runs; each day with rotation.dailyChance one unmet, unhired wanderer retires without a death notice and a fresh FWGC++-style wanderer replaces it; below W the tick tops up. A new wanderer is made in four steps (CreateSpecialHero from a template of the pool, AdjustEquipments, ChangeState(Active), EnterSettlementAction), keeps its FWGC++ sex and an epithet; the pool is the installed templates minus backstoryUnsafe, distinct within a culture where possible, with a recorded cross-culture fallback. A runtime wanderer takes its name, epithet and sex from campaign.json wandererReserve: per presentation culture of the towns, reserve FWGC++ residents of its civilizations (sex as the residents', names no other hero carries) with an archetypal FWGC++ epithet (one two or more of the world's people carry; else the template's) (MMR-281)",
  "sources": [
